    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug in the frai CLI. The issue was in how the `gate` command was passing arguments to the frai-gate subprocess.\n\n**The Problem:** \nWhen running `frai gate init --ci`, the `--ci` flag wasn't being passed through to frai-gate, so the GitHub Actions workflow file wasn't being created.\n\n**The Root Cause:**\nThe action handler for the `gate` command was relying on commander.js's variadic argument parsing (`[args...]`), which wasn't capturing the `--ci` flag correctly.\n\n**The Fix:**\nChanged the command handler at `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts:753` to use `process.argv.slice(3)` directly instead of relying on the `args` parameter from commander. This ensures all arguments after `frai gate` (including the `--ci` flag) are passed through to frai-gate.\n\n**Verification:**\n\u2705 Ran `frai gate init --ci` in a test directory  \n\u2705 Both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` were created successfully  \n\u2705 The workflow file contains the correct GitHub Actions configuration",
